[issue_comment] khancyr | created=2016-12-18T21:29:25Z | updated=2016-12-18T21:30:24Z | https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/pull/5404#issuecomment-267848145
What I am thinking is something like 
````
template <class FloatOne, class FloatTwo>
typename std::enable_if< (std::is_integral<FloatOne>::value ),  bool>::type is_equal(const FloatOne v_1, const FloatTwo v_2)
{
    return v_1 == v_2;
}

template <class FloatOne, class FloatTwo>
typename std::enable_if< (std::is_floating_point<FloatOne>::value), bool>::type  is_equal(const FloatOne v_1, const FloatTwo v_2)
{
    return fabsf(v_1 - v_2) < std::numeric_limits<decltype(v_1 - v_2)>::epsilon();
}

````

But it is bothering me that it is "template <class FloatOne, class FloatTwo>" and I can only make ````std::enable_if< (std::is_floating_point<FloatOne>::value), bool>::type```` working, I cannot find a solution with FloatOne and FloatTwo inside enable_if ...

